hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"256","Two words are light on the tongue, weigh heavily in the balance, and are loved by the Most Merciful One: Subḥānallāhi wa biḥamdih, Subḥānallāhi ‘l-`Aẓīm. Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said: Two words are light on the tongue, weigh heavily in the balance, and are loved by the Most Merciful One: Glorified is Allah and praised is He, Glorified is Allah the Most Great. Reference: Al-Bukhari 7/168, Muslim 4/2072."
"257","Wa qāla ṣallā Allāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam: La-an aqūla (subḥān Allāhi, wa-l-ḥamdu lillāhi, wa lā ilāha illā Allāhu, wa-Llāhu akbaru), aḥabbu ilayya mimmā ṭalaʿat ʿalayhi sh-shamsu.. And he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \To say (Glory be to Allah"," all praise is due to Allah"," there is no god but Allah"," and Allah is the Greatest) is more beloved to me than everything upon which the sun rises.\"""""
